       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 1,700 mg three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. The extended-release maximum is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** The ordered dose is about twice the maximum. That raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day), or\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily, or\n- Another dose?\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and include a note with the clinical rationale. I'll enter it as written."
